"父" = "Father";
"父\nここまでの戦いを、手帳に書き足しておいた。\n速く答えられた場所も、時間がかかった場所もある。これは優劣ではなく、戻る場所を探すための記録だ。" = "Father\nI added the battles so far to the notebook.\nSome places you answered quickly, and some took time. This is not a record of better or worse. It is a record for finding where to return.";
"父「B♭は大地の響きだ。足元の音を信じよう。重くても、支えになる。」\n土輪の門番「遠回りに見えても、ここまで来た音は無駄じゃない。中心へ行くなら、その積み重ねが要る。」" = "Father: \"B♭ is the resonance of the earth. Trust the sound under your feet. Even if it is heavy, it will support you.\"\nEarth-Ring Gatekeeper: \"It may look like a detour, but none of the sounds that brought you here were wasted. To reach the center, you need that accumulation.\"";
"父「DとAは近い。近いからこそ、急がなくていい。中で根が決まれば、指は追いつく。」\n裂け目の声「雷が落ちても、砂時計は止まらない。」" = "Father: \"D and A are close. Because they are close, you do not need to rush. Once the root is settled inside, your fingers will follow.\"\nVoice of the Rift: \"Even when thunder falls, the hourglass does not stop.\"";
"父「Eは柔らかい。Bは硬い。違いを間違えてもいい。戻って選び直せば、ちゃんと身につく。」\n廃路の職人「灰塔へ続く道を開ける。通るなら、音を濁すな。」" = "Father: \"E is soft. B is hard. It is fine to mistake the difference. Return and choose again, and it will become yours.\"\nCraftsman of the Old Road: \"I will open the road to the Gray Tower. If you pass, do not cloud the sound.\"";
"父「Fの水路は帰り道にも似ている。休むことも、進むための技だよ。」\n水門守「無理に進むな。息を整える技を覚えていけ。長い道になる。」" = "Father: \"The F waterway is like a road home. Resting is also a skill for moving forward.\"\nSluice Keeper: \"Do not force your way ahead. Learn a skill to steady your breath. The road will be long.\"";
"父「Gは風みたいに動く。見失いそうなら、Cで覚えた帰る感じを思い出そう。」\n風見台の少年「港の子だろ。こんな早くここまで来るなんて、風より速いな。」" = "Father: \"G moves like the wind. If you feel you might lose it, remember the sense of returning you learned at C.\"\nBoy at the Windwatch Platform: \"You are the child from the harbor, right? Getting here this fast makes you quicker than the wind.\"";
"父「ここからは、本当に自分の道だ。私は外で核の乱れを押さえている。行っておいで。」\n険路の声「鋭い六つを越えよ。見える道ではなく、戻る道を持つ者だけが通る。」" = "Father: \"From here, this is truly your path. I will hold back the disturbance of the core from outside. Go on.\"\nVoice of the Steep Path: \"Cross the sharp six. Only those who carry a road back, not a visible road, may pass.\"";
"父「ここから先は、自分の調律で進めばいい。私はここで聴いている。」" = "Father: \"From here on, move forward with your own tuning. I will be listening from here.\"";
"父「ここから先へ、私は入れない。でも、戻ってきた音は、ここまで残っている。」\n旧友の声「来たか。見えないまま、ここまで。なら見せてみろ。戻る道が、この沈黙に届くのか。」" = "Father: \"I cannot enter beyond this point. But the sounds you returned with remain here.\"\nOld Friend's Voice: \"So you came. All this way without seeing. Then show me. Can your road back reach this silence?\"";
"父「ここが灯火港だ。この音鍵は、まず帰る場所を知るところから始まる。焦らなくていいよ。」\n港の老人「屋久の環と呼ばれた古い島だ。最近、調律を乱された生き物が増えている。」" = "Father: \"This is Lamplight Harbor. This sound key begins with knowing where to return. You do not need to rush.\"\nHarbor Elder: \"This old island was once called the Ring of Yaku. Lately, more creatures have had their tuning disturbed.\"";
"父「ここは二つの根が重なる最初の洞だ。Cへ戻る感じを、胸の中に少し残しておこう。」\n洞守「灯と風がぶつかる日は、音鍵を持つ者が頼りだ。」" = "Father: \"This is the first cave where two roots overlap. Keep a little of the feeling of returning to C in your chest.\"\nCave Keeper: \"On days when lamp and wind collide, we rely on the one who carries the sound key.\"";
"父「この拠点の音を、いっしょに確かめよう。」" = "Father: \"Let us check the sound of this outpost together.\"";
"父「中心の影が近い。怖くなったら、ここまで戻ってきた音を思い出せばいい。」\n庭守「夕、黄、土、水。どれも止めるためではなく、中心へ送るためにある。」" = "Father: \"The shadow of the center is close. If fear comes, remember the sounds that brought you back this far.\"\nGarden Keeper: \"Evening, yellow, earth, and water. None are here to stop you. They are here to send you toward the center.\"";
"父「乾いた音は急がせてくる。でも、手は急がなくても届くよ。」\n砂鐘守「砂鐘の音が濁っている。君の音で、もう一度だけ澄ませてくれ。」" = "Father: \"Dry sounds try to hurry you. But your hand can reach them without rushing.\"\nSandbell Keeper: \"The sound of the sandbell is clouded. Let your sound clear it once more.\"";
"父「光に驚いたら、目を細めるみたいに音も少し絞ろう。根はちゃんと残っている。」\n塔番「父上と同じ構えだな。けれど、音は君自身のものだ。」" = "Father: \"If the light startles you, narrow the sound a little, like narrowing your eyes. The root is still there.\"\nTower Watcher: \"You hold yourself like your father. But the sound is your own.\"";
"父「冷えた音ほど輪郭は鋭い。指先を急がせないで、根の形を見てからでいい。」\n灰氷の声「ここまで来たなら、もう外周だけの子ではない。」" = "Father: \"The colder the sound, the sharper its outline. Do not rush your fingertips. You can wait until you know the shape of the root.\"\nVoice of Gray Ice: \"If you have come this far, you are no longer only a child of the outer ring.\"";
"父「力を抜くことも戦いだよ。Fの流れに乗れば、B♭の重さも怖くない。」\n水路守「息を整えろ。中心まで、休まず行ける者はいない。」" = "Father: \"Letting go of force is also part of the fight. If you ride the flow of F, the weight of B♭ will not frighten you.\"\nWaterway Keeper: \"Steady your breath. No one reaches the center without rest.\"";
"父「四つの根が揺れる。私は外側で道を保っている。自分の速さで進めばいい。」\n郭の碑「速さだけでは抜けられない。戻る根を持つ者だけが通る。」" = "Father: \"Four roots are swaying. I will hold the path from outside. Move at your own speed.\"\nWard Monument: \"Speed alone cannot pass. Only those who hold a root to return to may go through.\"";
"父「夕影は優しい。だから迷いやすい。迷ったら、最初の一音に戻ろう。」\n庭の影「ここまでの旅で、その音は少し静かになった。」" = "Father: \"Evening shadow is gentle. That is why it is easy to lose your way. If you are unsure, return to the first sound.\"\nGarden Shadow: \"Through the journey so far, that sound has become a little quieter.\"";
"父「夕影は優しいけれど、優しさは迷いにもなる。迷ったら、戻ればいい。」\n夕影の衛士「ここまで来たなら、もう戻るだけの旅ではないな。」" = "Father: \"Evening shadow is gentle, but gentleness can also become confusion. If you are unsure, return.\"\nEvening-Shadow Guard: \"If you have come this far, this is no longer only a journey of returning.\"";
"父「始まりの近くに見えて、もう始まりではない。ここまで積んだ音が、ちゃんと支えている。」\n塞の声「港へ戻る者か、中心へ向かう者か。迷った時の戻り方で分かる。」" = "Father: \"It may look close to the beginning, but it is no longer the beginning. The sounds you have built up are supporting you.\"\nVoice of the Fort: \"One who returns to the harbor, or one who goes to the center. You can tell by how they return when they are lost.\"";
"父「始まりへ戻る道だ。戻ることは後退じゃない。Cをもう一度、新しく聞こう。」\n帰路の灯「港の灯は、出発だけでなく帰還も照らす。」" = "Father: \"This is the road back to the beginning. Returning is not retreat. Listen to C again, as something new.\"\nLight of the Return Road: \"The harbor light shines not only on departures, but on returns.\"";
"父「島の反対側まで来たね。知らないはずの音でも、戻る場所があれば手は落ち着く。怖がらなくていい。」\n氷鏡の番人「港の灯が、こんな遠くまで届くとは思わなかった。」" = "Father: \"You have come to the far side of the island. Even for sounds you should not know yet, your hand can settle if it has a place to return. Do not be afraid.\"\nIce-Mirror Guardian: \"I did not think the harbor light could reach this far.\"";
"父「島の裏側まで来たね。遠く感じても、鍵盤の上では同じ十二の中にある。」\n氷鏡の番人「港の灯が、こんな底まで届くとは思わなかった。」" = "Father: \"You have reached the back side of the island. Even if it feels far away, on the keyboard it is still within the same twelve.\"\nIce-Mirror Guardian: \"I did not think the harbor light could reach this deep.\"";
"父「水の街では、音がやわらかく揺れる。急がず、ひとつ選べばいい。」\n庭師「水面がまた静かになった。あなたが通った跡だ。」" = "Father: \"In the water town, sound sways softly. Do not rush. Choose one.\"\nGardener: \"The water surface is quiet again. That is the trace you left.\"";
"父「濁った音の中でも、根は消えない。取り直す時間は、ちゃんとある。」\n市場の女主人「あの人は昔から、見える者だけが門をくぐれるのはおかしいと言っていたよ。」" = "Father: \"Even in clouded sound, the root does not disappear. There is time to take it again.\"\nMarket Mistress: \"That person always said it was wrong that only those who could see were allowed through the gate.\"";
"父「硬い音に当たっても、怖がらなくていい。少しずつ、少しずつ形になる。」\n工房の職人「その音鍵、ずいぶん古い型だな。普通は扱いづらいはずだが、妙に手に馴染んでいる。」" = "Father: \"Even when you meet a hard sound, you do not need to fear it. Little by little, it will take shape.\"\nWorkshop Craftsman: \"That sound key is an old model. It should be difficult to handle, but somehow it fits your hand.\"";
"父「私は外周の乱れを押さえている。大丈夫、ここは一人で入れる。風が砂に変わる瞬間を、よく聞いておいで。」\n砂鐘守「昔、父上と旅をした男もここで立ち止まった。耳の差で道を分けるな、と怒っていた。」" = "Father: \"I am holding back the disturbance of the outer ring. You will be all right. You can enter here alone. Listen closely to the moment when wind becomes sand.\"\nSandbell Keeper: \"Long ago, the man who traveled with your father stopped here too. He was angry that the road was divided by differences of ear.\"";
"父「色に引かれそうになったら、いちど息をしよう。いま鳴っている根だけでいい。」\n水脈の番人「その音で水面が落ち着いた。次は奥へ行けるはずだ。」" = "Father: \"If color starts to pull you, take one breath. Only the root sounding now matters.\"\nGuardian of the Water Vein: \"That sound calmed the surface. You should be able to go deeper now.\"";
"父「落ちる感覚に引かれそうなら、手元へ戻ろう。鍵盤はいつも近くにある。」\n斜坑の声「砂、雷、水、灰。四つを覚えるな。今の一つを選べ。」" = "Father: \"If the feeling of falling starts to pull you in, return to your hands. The keyboard is always close.\"\nVoice of the Inclined Shaft: \"Sand, thunder, water, gray. Do not memorize all four. Choose the one that is here now.\"";
"父「重い六つは足を止める。でも、積んできた音はもう沈まない。ゆっくりでも進める。」\n険路の声「重い六つを越えよ。港から来た子よ、ここまで戻ってきた手順を信じろ。」" = "Father: \"The heavy six may stop your feet. But the sounds you have built up will not sink now. You can move forward, even slowly.\"\nVoice of the Steep Path: \"Cross the heavy six. Child from the harbor, trust the steps that returned you this far.\"";
"父「重い音は、押す前の時間をくれる。焦らなくていい。戻ってから選ぼう。」\n門番「遠回りに見える道ほど、中心では役に立つ。」" = "Father: \"A heavy sound gives you time before you press. Do not rush. Return, then choose.\"\nGatekeeper: \"The roads that look like detours are the ones that help most at the center.\"";
"父「鏡に映るものに惑わされても、覚えた根は消えないよ。」\n鏡庭の声「遠い町から来た音が、ここで静かに形を結ぶ。」" = "Father: \"Even if the mirror confuses you, the root you learned will not disappear.\"\nVoice of the Mirror Garden: \"A sound from a distant town quietly takes shape here.\"";
"父「霧の中では、ゆっくりでいい。外の揺らぎより、戻れる根を信じよう。」\n霧晶の娘「霧の向こうから音がした。あなたの音だったのね。」" = "Father: \"In the mist, slow is fine. Trust the root you can return to more than the shaking outside.\"\nMistcrystal Girl: \"I heard a sound from beyond the mist. It was your sound.\"";
"父「霧の中では、足元が少し遅れてくる。先に決めるのは根だ。大丈夫、戻れば進める。」\n沈橋の声「足元が消えても、最初に握った鍵の感触までは消えない。」" = "Father: \"In the mist, your footing comes a little late. The root is what you decide first. It is all right. If you return, you can move forward.\"\nVoice of the Sunken Bridge: \"Even if the ground underfoot disappears, the feel of the first key you held will not.\"";
"父「静かな場所ほど、正解は隠れる。急がなくていい。根を決めてから進もう。」\n水殿の柱「音を急がせる者は沈む。根を決めた者だけが渡る。」" = "Father: \"The quieter the place, the more the right answer hides. Do not rush. Decide the root, then move forward.\"\nPillar of the Water Hall: \"Those who hurry sound will sink. Only those who decide the root may cross.\"";
"父が手帳の記録から、迷いやすい音の生き物の影を示す。これは戦いではなく、何度でも戻るための稽古。" = "Father shows shadows of Aura Creatures that cause hesitation based on notebook records. This is not battle, but practice for returning again and again.";
